  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mazi - Support CSO</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Collaboration and partnerships with NGOs, especially those who are active at the Greek/European borders, and/or who work daily withpeople on the move, e.g. in camps, during asylum procedures, undocumented people are important for a successful Oxfam Novib approach. These organizations are the ears and eyes of what&#x2019;s going on at the borders. As Oxfam Novib we can use the evidence for our advocacy and campaigning work, to show politicians at European and national level what migration can lead to politically and show the public how people on the move are treated. The grants to be provided to 4 selected NGOs &#x2013; after a careful application procedure &#x2013; will help the NGOs to continue their work in Greece and will make it possible to provide Oxfam Novib with the necessary input on human rights violations for advocacy and campaigning work. The fund comes from internal and unrestricted funding Safe Unit</narrative>
  </description>
